From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:37:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 76/99] v8: e2k: ask for the trap PC only of protected memory
 accesses

Asking the instruction layer for the PC of an instruction closes its
scheduling window. The code generator asked for it at every load and
store, while only accesses with a protected access mode (wasm out of
bounds and null checks by the trap handler) record it. With WebAssembly
enabled this broke the windows of ordinary JS loads and stores: props
+6 % and alloc +12 % against the same tree without wasm (bench.js,
Elbrus-8SV). Accesses with kMemoryAccessDirect now pass no PC pointer;
without WebAssembly none does.
